<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roger Casement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1916</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roger Casement was an Irish-born British consul whose 1904 report on atrocities in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a>, and later on the Putumayo region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, made him a leading humanitarian. Turning to Irish nationalism, he sought German help for an Irish rising, was arrested on landing in Ireland in 1916 and was hanged for treason in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p></div>
